+-- Guarded T0 claim (AD-14): the cadence's first step. Atomic status
+-- transition (queued -> contact_initiated) + form-token mint + attempt
+-- append + next-step, in ONE statement. Only fires when the row is still
+-- queued at attempt_count 0; a concurrent writer or a retry that already
+-- advanced returns 0 rows and the caller stands down (no duplicate T0 —
+-- the no-duplicate-T0 test pins the next_attempt_at advance).
+--
+-- The form_token is minted here (rc3-5 owns the T0 mint — creation stamps
+-- none, form_handler:101). The sweep mints a ~288-bit token
+-- (wisp.random_string(48), the insert_erasure_token precedent), SENDS the
+-- invite carrying it, then claims — stamping the token + a 10-day TTL (A3,
+-- covers the 6-day cadence) in the same guarded write. Send-then-claim
+-- ordering: worst case under a concurrent T0 is a duplicate invite (one
+-- with a dead token), never a missing one — preferable to claim-first,
+-- where a crash after claim but before send would skip the invite entirely.
+--
+-- The next horizon is computed from the row's CURRENT next_attempt_at +
+-- the step increment (not created_at): a re-enabled row re-arms
+-- next_attempt_at = now(), so the cadence follows that anchor, and adding
+-- to next_attempt_at keeps the cadence self-healing after downtime.
+UPDATE reference_call
+SET status                 = 'contact_initiated',
+    form_token             = $2,
+    form_token_expires_at  = now() + interval '10 days',
+    attempts               = attempts || $3::jsonb,
+    attempt_count          = attempt_count + 1,
+    next_attempt_at        = next_attempt_at + ($4 * interval '1 hour'),
+    updated_at             = now()
+WHERE id = $1
+  AND status = 'queued'
+  AND attempt_count = 0
+RETURNING id::text;
